# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build outputs
#
# CAREFUL: a bare `build/` also matches *source* directories named "build" at
# any depth — including the `com.omnideck.build` package that holds every
# convention plugin. That silently drops real source from commits and only
# surfaces on a fresh clone, as a "Could not find implementation class" failure
# in CI. Keep the negation below, or anchor any new pattern you add.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
!**/src/**/build/
.gradle/
out/
captures/
.cxx/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local configuration — never commit machine-specific overrides or secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local.properties
*.keystore
*.jks
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated reports / baselines produced by CI, not authored by hand
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/detekt-baseline.xml
**/lint-baseline.xml
**/*.hprof

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kotlin/Native, KSP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.kotlin/

# Scratch gradle output redirected to a file (./gradlew build *> build_log.txt).
*_log.txt
/*.txt
!/CMakeLists.txt

# Play upload key must never live in the repo (§12.3 of the internal architecture
# baseline) — CI injects it from KMS/secrets, never from a file here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal planning documents — deliberately not published.
#
# These stay on developer machines and in internal storage. Source comments
# still cite them by section number (e.g. "architecture.md §5.1"); that is a
# pointer into the internal document, not a file you will find in this repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/architecture.md
/implementation_plan.md
/docs/adr/
